{
  "slug": "brightspeed-reconciliation",
  "title": "Brightspeed: reconcile FCC availability with the build story",
  "lede": "The full 20-state filing count is 1.79 million residential-capable FTTP locations. Brightspeed separately reported more than 3 million fiber-enabled locations in April 2026. Geography explains part of the original shortfall; the remaining definitions still need an address-level bridge.",
  "scope": "Public research as of September 20, 2026. FCC availability as of December 31, 2025; current retained file revision September 15, 2026. Company figures are dated reported measures, not audited equivalence to FCC locations.",
  "pages": [
    "states",
    "rightfiber"
  ],
  "type": "Measurement reconciliation",
  "asOf": "2026-09-20",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "answer",
      "title": "The public build story is larger than the FCC availability count",
      "nav": "Conclusion",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Brightspeed reported more than 3 million fiber-enabled locations on April 2, 2026. A fresh count of every current D25 provider file for Connect Holding II LLC, provider 470022, produces 1,793,485 unique technology-50 residential-capable locations across 20 states. These are different dated measures; neither should replace the other without a location-and-unit bridge. [P01] [FCCCAT]",
        "The FCC count now covers every state listed for this verified filer. That resolves the prior geographical omission, but does not prove that no additional legal filer should be included. No additional filer increment has been established by the reviewed corporate records. Legacy CenturyLink or United Telephone names alone are insufficient. [P09] [P12]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge",
      "title": "What the expanded FCC reconciliation actually explains",
      "nav": "Count reconciliation",
      "table": {
        "columns": [
          "Step",
          "R/X FTTP locations",
          "Interpretation"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Existing 15-state atlas subtotal",
            "1,681,717",
            "D25; mixed retained revisions. It was a scoped subtotal, not the full 20-state filer count."
          ],
          [
            "Add Georgia, Mississippi, New Jersey, Oklahoma and Wisconsin",
            "+111,769",
            "Newly covered states:15,320;3,649;39,793;23;52,984 respectively. [FCC13] [FCC28] [FCC34] [FCC40] [FCC55]"
          ],
          [
            "Refresh retained North Carolina input",
            "\u22121",
            "Current provider file yields 463,300 versus prior 463,301; a filing-revision difference, not a construction estimate. [FCC37]"
          ],
          [
            "Current 20-state filer union",
            "1,793,485",
            "All 20 mixed-technology provider files validated against catalog raw-row counts. Technology 50 R/X location IDs globally deduplicated; no cross-state duplicate IDs found."
          ],
          [
            "Add business-only locations outside R/X",
            "0",
            "For these 20 files, the unique all-service FTTP set equals the R/X set. Business-only filtering does not explain a positive gap in this measured filer."
          ],
          [
            "Compare company reported thresholds",
            "Unreconciled",
            "October 3, 2025: more than 2.5 million locations reached; April 2, 2026: more than 3 million fiber-enabled locations. Dates, units and readiness definitions differ. No implied overstatement or under-filing finding. [P05] [P01]"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "paragraphs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "hypotheses",
      "title": "Test the remaining explanations without inventing a multiplier",
      "nav": "Open bridge",
      "table": {
        "columns": [
          "Potential explanation",
          "What is established",
          "What remains necessary"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Geographic omission",
            "Five omitted states add 111,769 locations.",
            "Geography explains this portion of the former subtotal difference, not the remaining company-to-FCC gap."
          ],
          [
            "Filing vintage and construction timing",
            "D25 availability is December 31, 2025; September 2026 is the file revision. April 2026 is a later company milestone. [P01] [P18]",
            "Comparable monthly state/location cohorts; lower-bound milestone differences are not exact build additions."
          ],
          [
            "Buildings versus dwelling units",
            "FCC BSLs represent structures; an MDU can have multiple units under one BSL. [P15]",
            "Brightspeed\u2019s counting definition and a same-location Fabric unit-count join. No supported Brightspeed-specific multiplier yet."
          ],
          [
            "Passed versus installable",
            "The January 2025 release gives approximately 1.82 million passings and separately describes immediate installations for hundreds of thousands. It does not reconcile those populations. [P02]",
            "Property/address readiness, service-order eligibility, final drops and acceptance dates. Do not quantify a readiness gap from broad marketing language."
          ],
          [
            "Additional subsidiaries or legal filers",
            "Connect Holding II is the verified current catalog filer. Group legal entities include legacy ILECs and fiber affiliates. [FCCCAT] [P12] [P14]",
            "Documented additional provider IDs plus deduplicated location sets; no automatic addition of retained Lumen assets."
          ],
          [
            "Inherited fiber counted twice",
            "Brightspeed reported 200,000 existing fiber-enabled addresses at launch. [P08]",
            "Confirm inclusion in each later milestone before adding or subtracting the inherited base."
          ],
          [
            "RDOF reporting validation",
            "January 9, 2026 letter describes potential milestone issues in eight states. [P06]",
            "Its serviceability/Fabric-ID caveat is RDOF-specific and does not allocate a platform-wide residual."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "paragraphs": []
    },
