    {
      "id": "entities",
      "title": "Use the right corporate perimeter",
      "nav": "Entity map",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The 20-state Lumen ILEC transaction closed October 3, 2022. FCC approval was adopted and released August 19; Lumen announced approval August 22. Approval and closing are separate dates. [P09] [P10] [P11]",
        "The December 2023 FCC ruling places Connect Holding II beneath Connect Holding, then Connect Midco, Connect Intermediate and Connect Parent. It calls Connect Holding II immediate parent of ten wireless licensees; that does not make it direct parent of every operating company. [P12]",
        "Lumen retained national fiber routes and associated networks, along with ILEC operations in 16 states. Do not move retained Lumen, Qwest or Level 3 assets into Brightspeed by name similarity. [P11]",
        "South Carolina approved selected affiliate fiber-asset transfers and leasebacks on August 14, 2026. The order does not prove consummation, exact-span title or implementation in all 20 states. The April 17 application provides Fiber Connection and Fiber Services name histories, including June 2, 2025 changes. These entity changes establish no extra FCC locations by themselves. [P13] [P14]"
      ]
    },
